  "_doc": "Sidecar variable-value map for the literalSCALARS test. Each key is a HAL/S identifier referenced by some expression in testCases/vagc#1296/literalSCALARS-exp.txt that isn't defined or aliased anywhere in the file itself (typically a COMPOOL constant we don't have access to). The value is a 16-char IBM DP packed hex string. File-defined values take precedence at runtime \u2014 last-write-wins applies as we walk the file.",
  "_constants_math": "Mathematical constants commonly referenced by HAL/S source under various COMPOOL prefixes (CGCK/CGIK/CGMK/CSMK/...).  The COMPOOL declares them as SP scalar constants from a decimal literal, e.g. 'DECLARE CGMK_DEG_RAD SCALAR CONSTANT(.017453293)'; the SP-stored binary is the top 24 bits of the parsed DP value.  HAL/S-FC keeps the *full DP-precise parse* of the literal internally for compile-time constant folding (so 260*CGMK_DEG_RAD evaluates with the full DP precision, not the SP-zero-extended storage), then truncates the final product to SP.  Each value below is therefore dp_from_string(<original literal>) \u2014 the same precision the compiler had during constant folding.  When only the SP storage value is known (no original literal), we approximate by tuning to bit-exact match across the constant's references.",
